---
import Editorial from '../layouts/Editorial.astro';
import { analytics } from '../config/integrations';
import { legalPolicy } from '../config/legal';
---

<Editorial
  title="Your setup. Your privacy."
  description="What this edition of Tagrivo stores, what the interactive tools do with your inputs, and what changes when you visit another website."
>
  <p>
    <strong>Last updated: October 30, 2026.</strong>
  </p>
  {legalPolicy.approved ? (
    <section class="helper" aria-label="Person responsible for data processing">
      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>{legalPolicy.operator.name}</strong>, DNI {legalPolicy.operator.document},
        administers Tagrivo from Peru under the personal brand JC Labs. Tagrivo is an independent
        editorial project; neither brand is presented as an incorporated company.
      </p>
      <p>Address for correspondence and privacy requests: {legalPolicy.operator.address}.</p>
      <p>
        Contact: <a href="mailto:hello.jclabs@gmail.com">hello.jclabs@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  ) : (
    <p class="helper">
      <strong>Provisional notice for a preview edition.</strong> This page describes the current
      implementation; it is not presented as a finalized legal privacy policy. Tagrivo is the
      editorial brand, administered by an individual in Peru under JC Labs, a personal brand for
      digital projects. Neither name represents an incorporated company. The audience is primarily
      in the United States. Required legal identity and address information for the person
      responsible for data processing has not been supplied for publication. This notice therefore
      remains provisional and search indexing remains disabled.
    </p>
  )}
  <h2>The information you enter</h2>
  <p>
    The Printer Finder and cost calculator run in your browser. This edition has no account system,
    user database, contact-submission form, newsletter signup, or advertising pixel. The Finder has
    a local interactive form, not a server submission endpoint. Its controls remain disabled until
    its browser handler is ready. Calculator inputs and comparison quotes remain in page memory.
  </p>
  <p>
    Closing or refreshing a tool normally resets its inputs. New links from the home page pass the
    selected platform in a URL fragment (after #), which is not included in the HTTP request. The
    Finder reads and clears that handoff without storing it. Older links with a platform query
    parameter still work: the initial request can reach hosting logs before the tool clears the
    parameter. Comparison links contain public printer IDs, not cost quotes. Those query URLs can
    appear in browser history, shared links and hosting requests. Do not put personal information in
    URLs.
  </p>
  <h2>A theme preference on your device</h2>
  <p>
    The site uses browser local storage for a light or dark theme preference under the key{' '}
    <strong>tagrivo-theme</strong>. This is not an advertising identifier. You can remove it through
    your browser's site-data controls. If local storage is unavailable, the site still works.
  </p>
  <p>
    The application does not set advertising cookies or load Amazon tracking scripts. Opening an
    ordinary affiliate link takes you to Amazon, where its own practices apply.
  </p>
  <h2>Optional analytics and your choice</h2>
  {analytics.enabled ? (
    <>
      <p>
        Google Analytics loads only after you choose Allow analytics. Declining leaves the tools and
        affiliate links available without this measurement. It records page visits and identified
        product-link clicks. Events omit URL query strings, fragments, tool answers, email content
        and customer information. This version also omits referrer values; it does not promise
        complete campaign or organic-source attribution. Search Console supplies search reports
        separately.
      </p>
      <p>
        Google receives technical connection information and can set analytics cookies after
        permission. This is not anonymous or cookie-free measurement. Advertising signals and
        personalization are disabled. A consent preference, tagrivo-analytics-consent, is stored
        locally for up to 30 days. Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control prevent this measurement.
        Use{' '}
        <a href="#analytics-preferences" data-analytics-settings>
          Analytics preferences
        </a>{' '}
        to withdraw permission. Revocation reloads the page and clears this integration's host
        cookies; it cannot retract data already received by Google. Contact us about applicable data
        rights.
      </p>
    </>
  ) : (
    <p>
      Google Analytics is not active in this edition because no measurement destination has been
      connected. No Google tag, analytics cookies or analytics-consent storage are used by the
      active application. The integration is prepared for a real destination, policy review and
      prior reader consent; it will not load a tracker simply because you visit this page. The only
      active localStorage preference is tagrivo-theme. The site does not use sessionStorage.
    </p>
  )}
  <h2>Fonts, images, and downloaded estimates</h2>
  <p>
    Site fonts and displayed images are served as site assets rather than loaded from an external
    font or image tracking service. Downloading a cost estimate creates a CSV file locally in your
    browser; this does not submit the estimate to Tagrivo.
  </p>
  <h2>Hosting and ordinary web requests</h2>
  <p>
    Serving a website requires requests that can include an IP address, requested URL, browser
    information, and timestamps. The hosting provider may process request logs for delivery,
    security, and reliability under its own policies. This application does not expose or maintain a
    separate user database. A static Astro build does not eliminate the hosting provider's
    processing of technical requests. We do not claim that visiting this site involves no personal
    data processing.
  </p>
  <p>
    Tagrivo is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Consult{' '}
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      Cloudflare's privacy policy
    </a>{' '}
    for provider-level information. Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend St., San Francisco, CA 94107,
    United States, can process traffic and security information and make service statistics or logs
    available under the account's settings. This application has no separate log-export service or
    visitor database. Technical-data retention follows the provider's service-specific policies for
    delivery, security and legal obligations; the 12-month correspondence rule below does not set
    Cloudflare's log-retention period. Search Console, already verified for this property, supplies
    search-performance reports; verification does not install an analytics tag.
  </p>
  <p>
    Cloudflare may use security cookies when its protection features require them, as described in
    its{' '}
    <a
      href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/reference/policies-compliances/cloudflare-cookies/"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      cookie documentation
    </a>
    . These provider features and their account settings are separate from the application. We do
    not promise that every visitor, browser or security challenge receives no cookies.
  </p>
  <h2>Manufacturer and retailer links</h2>
  <p>
    When you follow a link to another website, that site receives a request from your browser and
    applies its own policies. Its cookies, accounts, or purchase records are outside this site's
    local tools. Amazon affiliate links include a public tracking ID that can support referral
    attribution. We do not embed Amazon images, advertising pixels or purchase widgets. See our{' '}
    <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Clicking a product link opens a direct Amazon URL containing the product ASIN and our Store ID,
    tagrivo-20. The link suppresses the browser referrer with noreferrer. Amazon still receives the
    destination request, including technical connection information and any Amazon cookies the
    browser sends. Tagrivo does not send Finder answers or calculator values in that link or receive
    checkout details through the website code. When optional analytics is active and you have
    allowed it, an identified link click can generate the limited product-click event described
    above.
  </p>
  <p>
    Amazon handles information after you visit it under its{' '}
    <a
      href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/help/customer/display.html?nodeId=GX7NJQ4ZB8MHFRNJ"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      privacy notice
    </a>
    . Its cookies and purchase records are not controlled by the Finder or calculator.
  </p>
  <h2>Contact and email messages</h2>
  <p>
    For privacy enquiries or editorial correspondence, email{' '}
    <a href="mailto:hello.jclabs@gmail.com">hello.jclabs@gmail.com</a>. If you email us, your sender
    address, message and any attachments are received through the Gmail mailbox to review and
    respond to your request. Contact opens a static page; its email link uses mailto to open your
    configured email application. A message is sent only if you send it there. The website has no
    message-submission form. Avoid sending shipping labels, customer addresses, credentials or other
    unnecessary private information. Providing correspondence is optional; without a way to reply,
    we may be unable to answer. We use messages only to answer enquiries, assess corrections and
    handle communications related to Tagrivo. We do not sell personal data or use those enquiries
    for advertising without permission.
  </p>
  <h2 id="email-retention">Email retention and your rights</h2>
  <p>
    The correspondence retention rule is <strong>12 months from the last communication</strong>,
    unless an applicable legal obligation requires a longer period or a deletion request calls for
    earlier review. The operator's procedure is a monthly manual review of Tagrivo correspondence
    and associated attachments. Deletion is not automated. Any legally required exception must be
    limited to the necessary records and documented.
  </p>
  <p>
    Gmail is provided by Google LLC, 1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043, United
    States. Google processes the mailbox under its{' '}
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      privacy policy
    </a>
    . Gmail and Cloudflare can process information internationally, including in the United States
    and other countries where their infrastructure and authorized service providers operate.
    Technical infrastructure is not promised to be located exclusively in Peru. Personal data is
    used for the purposes described here; it is not sold or used for unsolicited marketing by
    Tagrivo. Deleting a message from the mailbox does not promise immediate erasure from provider
    backups.
  </p>
  <p>
    To ask about your information or request access, correction, deletion or opposition to its use,
    write to <a href="mailto:hello.jclabs@gmail.com">hello.jclabs@gmail.com</a> with the subject
    “Tagrivo privacy request.” Identify the correspondence and action requested. We may need
    proportionate identity verification before disclosing or deleting information; do not send an
    identity document with an initial enquiry. Requests are handled manually. Applicable rights,
    including portability where required, are subject to Peru's Law No. 29733 and its regulation.
    You can also consult the{' '}
    <a href="https://www.gob.pe/anpd" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      Peruvian data protection authority
    </a>
    .
  </p>
  {!legalPolicy.approved && (
    <p>
      The public contact address and personal-brand names do not replace the responsible person's
      required legal identity and address. The final information notice, lawful grounds and any
      required consent or registration must be resolved before this is presented as a final policy.
      No personal name, home address or identification number is invented or published here.
    </p>
  )}
  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If this site adds data collection, analytics, forms, or advertising, the policy needs to
    describe the resulting practices before those features are introduced. The date above identifies
    this edition.
  </p>
  <p>
    See <a href="/contact/">contact and corrections</a> for editorial guidance.
  </p>
</Editorial>
